From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwmapi, uxtheme, winex11: Aero glass for Windows 7's shell

Purpose: Windows 7's taskbar and Start menu in Aero, over glass, instead of
Windows 7 Basic.
Windows 7 behavior: with desktop composition, explorer asks
DwmIsCompositionEnabled and uxtheme's IsCompositionActive, opens the
Aero theme's "...Composited" classes, draws its taskbar and Start menu with
their translucent images (buffered paint with alpha), and calls
DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow on them. The DWM blends such a window by the
alpha of its pixels over what is behind it, blurred, under the
colorization color (HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\DWM ColorizationColor,
the Aero theme's 0x6B74B8FC) and the glass's reflection (part 40 of the
theme's DWMWindow atlas). The clock draws with plain DrawThemeText: the
theme's Composited and TextGlow properties make uxtheme draw it with alpha
and a glow. The Show desktop button (ShowDesktop::Button) gives its glass
image for the whole class, which Windows takes before Button's push button
image: a class is searched whole (state, part, class) before the class it
overrides.
Wine before: DwmIsCompositionEnabled gave FALSE in the shell (0125, as on
Windows 7 Basic), IsCompositionActive was a stub that gave FALSE,
DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow returned E_NOTIMPL and DwmGetColorizationColor
E_NOTIMPL. Forcing composition on alone left the taskbar black (its window
surface sent X an opaque copy of pixels whose alpha is mostly 0), the clock
invisible (GDI text leaves alpha 0), and the Show desktop button an opaque
grey push button (uxtheme searched every class for the part before the
derived class's own class-wide properties). draw_composited_text read the
rows of a top-down DIB upside down (GetObject gives a positive height).
Change: in the Windows 7 shell's process, DwmIsCompositionEnabled gives
TRUE when the session sets WIN4WINE_AERO=1 (session.json "aero").
IsCompositionActive gives what DwmIsCompositionEnabled gives.
DwmGetColorizationColor gives the colorization color.
DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow, with composition, sets the window's
"__win4wine_glass" property to the colorization color and
"__win4wine_glass_reflection" to the reflection (decoded with WIC from the
theme file's atlas stream), and has its surface made again. winex11 gives
such a window an ARGB visual and a surface that keeps the alpha of its
pixels, puts the color and the reflection (stretched to a wider window)
under them at each flush, and sets _WIN4WINE_GLASS on its X window, for the
X compositor that blurs what is behind it. DrawThemeTextEx honours the
theme's Composited, TextGlow, TextGlowSize, GlowColor and GlowIntensity
and DTT_GLOWSIZE: composited text is drawn from its grayscale coverage over
a box-spread glow, in a DIB whose row order is probed. MSSTYLES_FindProperty
searches each class whole before the class it overrides.
Scope: composition only with WIN4WINE_AERO=1 in w7-explorer.exe, so only
it marks glass windows; the theme lookup order and the theme's composited
text apply to every program; the blur region is not kept (the whole window).
---
